<title>UK: UK's Halifax says house prices rise 0.5 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>UK's Halifax says house prices rise 0.5 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Halifax Building Society released the following seasonally adjusted UK house price data -</p>
<p> HOUSE PRICES (index base 1983=100)     Nov     Oct     Nov,95</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted index		 213.6   212.6   199.1</p>
<p> Monthly change (in pct)		     0.5     1.7    0.5</p>
<p> Annual change (in pct)			7.2     7.1   -1.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The Halifax said the stabilisation in the annual figures confirms its view that house price inflation is now likely to end the year at around 7.0 percent.</p>
<p>It said the last time the index reached the level of 213.6 was in January 1992, but the index is still 6.1 percent below its peak in May 1989.</p>
<p>Prices paid by first time buyers rose in November by 0.9 percent and the average price paid by first time buyers was 48,408 stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
